{"context_data":"{\n  \"target\": {\n    \"id\": \"mech_skill_generator_blueprint\",\n    \"human_name\": \"Skill Generator Blueprint DSL\",\n    \"type\": \"MECHANIC\",\n    \"layer\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n    \"intent\": \"To provide a fluent, builder-style interface for constructing skills while encapsulating the complexity of property initialization and SW-budget tracking.\",\n    \"logic\": \"- **Builder Pattern:** The `blueprint` struct tracks a `skill.Skill` instance.\\n- **Fluent Methods:** Provides methods like `addDamage()`, `setRange()`, `addStunChance()` that return the blueprint for chaining.\\n- **Internal Balancing:** Methods like `setRange()` and `addDamage()` handle the specific property keys and default values (e.g., setting LoS targeting by default).\\n- **PSW Reporting:** The `psw()` method provides real-time access to the skill's current Positive Skill Weight during the build process.\"\n  },\n  \"ancestry\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mech_skill_generator_core\",\n      \"human_name\": \"Skill Generator Core Mechanic\",\n      \"type\": \"MECHANIC\",\n      \"layer\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n      \"intent\": \"To implement the dispatcher logic that selects primary producers, layers secondary properties, and ensures the final skill satisfies grade-specific PSW bands and net-zero SW balance.\",\n      \"logic\": \"1. **Band Calculation:** Retrieve PSW range for the target grade from `gradeBand`.\\n2. **Primary Dispatch:** Randomly select an allowed primary producer (e.g., `melee`, `heal`).\\n3. **Secondary Layering:** Apply a secondary layer (e.g., `dot`, `aoe`) with grade-dependent probability.\\n4. **Cost Balancing:** Use `applyDelayCloser` to adjust the `Delay` property until the skill's net SW is exactly zero.\\n5. **Orchestration:** Pass the resulting skill to the classifier and name generator.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"module_skill_generator\",\n      \"human_name\": \"Skill Generator Module\",\n      \"type\": \"MODULE\",\n      \"layer\": \"ARCHITECTURE\",\n      \"intent\": \"To group and orchestrate the procedural generation, classification, and naming of skills within the Upsilon Hub ecosystem, ensuring grade-aware and tag-driven outputs.\",\n      \"logic\": \"The module acts as a high-level container for the following sub-components:\\n- **API Interface:** Defines how external services (like the character roll) request new skills.\\n- **Generator Core:** Handles the primary dispatching and budget logic.\\n- **Classifier:** Infers semantic tags from the final skill properties.\\n- **Name Generator:** Produces diegetic names based on the inferred tags.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"req_skill_generation\",\n      \"human_name\": \"Skill Generation System Requirement\",\n      \"type\": \"REQUIREMENT\",\n      \"layer\": \"BUSINESS\",\n      \"intent\": \"To specify that the skill roll pipeline must produce grade-aware, category-tagged skills with diegetic names, so a player understands what a skill does from its tag icons and name without opening a tooltip.\",\n      \"logic\": \"Every procedurally generated skill must satisfy four constraints:\\n\\n**1. Grade targeting** — the generator accepts a target grade (I–V) and produces a skill whose positive skill weight falls within the grade's PSW band (see `[[rule_skill_grading_system]]`). Grade I is the default.\\n\\n**2. Tag classification** — after generation, skills carry an ordered `tags []string` derived from their final properties (not authored). Tags drive icon composition, name prefix selection, and action-panel rendering. The 17-tag vocabulary covers behavior (`trap`, `counter`, `reaction`, `passive`), effect family (`heal`, `shield`, `dot`, `stun`, `buff`, `debuff`), delivery (`melee`, `ranged`, `aoe`), and modifiers (`crit`, `channeled`, `instant`, `mobility`).\\n\\n**3. Diegetic naming** — skill names follow a `[Modifier] [Subject] [Suffix]` template capped at 24 characters. No name may equal a raw property key (`Damage`, `Heal`, `Shield`).\\n\\n**4. Arena action panel** — equipped skills with `behavior ∈ {Direct, Reaction, Counter, Trap}` appear as clickable buttons in the Battle Arena action panel; skills with `behavior == Passive` render in a read-only passive rail below the active row.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirement_req_trpg_game_definition\",\n      \"human_name\": \"TRPG Game Definition\",\n      \"type\": \"REQUIREMENT\",\n      \"layer\": \"BUSINESS\",\n      \"intent\": \"Define Upsilon Battle as a turn-based Tactical RPG where players deploy character rosters onto a procedurally generated grid and compete via initiative-driven combat.\",\n      \"logic\": \"- **Genre:** Turn-based Tactical RPG (TRPG).\\n- **Core Loop:** Players deploy 3 characters onto a grid board. Characters act in order of initiative (delay-based ticker). On each turn, a character may Move, Attack, Pass, or Forfeit.\\n- **Board:** A procedurally generated rectangular grid (5-15 tiles per side) with obstacle tiles.\\n- **Teams:** Players are grouped into 2 opposing teams. Allies share a TeamID. Victory is achieved when all opposing entities are defeated or forfeit.\\n- **Action Economy:** Each action incurs a delay cost that determines when the character next acts. Move (+20/tile), Attack (+100), Pass (+300), Timeout (+400).\\n- **Shot Clock:** Each turn has a strict 30-second limit. Exceeding it triggers an auto-pass with penalty.\\n- **Modes:** 1v1 PvE, 1v1 PvP, 2v2 PvE, 2v2 PvP.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"dependents\": []\n}","instruction":"Analyze the provided Trace Context and generate a ~500-word summary organized as follows:\n1. Upper Context: Summarize the intent and logic of the ancestry. What high-level business goal are we fulfilling?\n2. Current Objective: Explain the intent of the target atom. Highlight its specific responsibility.\n3. Downward Impact: Look at the dependents. How does this atom's logic constrain or enable these descendants?\n\nFavor the current objective. If ancestry is thin, focus on the atom as a new root. If descendants are missing, treat it as a leaf-node.","system_objective":"You are an ATD Architect performing an impact assessment. Your goal is to provide a narrative summary of an atom's role in the vertical graph slice."}